# Line endings: LF everywhere, enforced on checkout and check-in.
*       text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads, opted out of text normalisation.
#
# These MUST come after the `*` rule above: in .gitattributes the LAST matching
# pattern wins, so a binary declaration placed first is silently overridden.
#
# The guard is not cosmetic. Git's `text=auto` heuristic calls a file text when
# it finds no NUL byte in the sampled prefix, and FITS headers are plain ASCII —
# two of the tracked .fits payloads sample clean and are seen as text, so
# `text=auto` alone would strip CR bytes out of binary image data and corrupt
# them. `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff`.

*.fits  binary
*.png   binary
